# packages/admin — environment
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; no secrets in the repo.
#   cp packages/admin/.env.example packages/admin/.env
#   pnpm --filter @nns/admin build
#   pnpm --filter @nns/admin start u <name> [awardee-address]
#   pnpm --filter @nns/admin start p <fee_standard> <fee_long> <commission_bp> <effective-height>
#   pnpm --filter @nns/admin start f <amount_luna>
#   pnpm --filter @nns/admin start a <name> <reserve_luna> <end-height>
#
# A U takes no effective height — it executes in the block it lands in (§6 U,
# r22). An A's end height is measured from the block it lands in, like a P's
# effective height, and gets the same hour of landing margin. All four are dry
# runs: they print what the message would do and send nothing. Append --send
# to broadcast.
#
# For `u` there is a shorter road: bin/nns-u writes this file if it is
# missing, builds what is stale, checks the node is reachable, in consensus
# and holding ADMIN_ADDRESS, and runs the command.
#
# Variable names match packages/indexer/.env.example on purpose — on a box
# that runs both, one set of values serves. The admin *private key* is
# deliberately not here: it lives in the node's wallet (importRawKey), and the
# CLI only unlocks it by address (docs/rpc-reference.md §5).

# ── RPC connection (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Either set NNS_RPC_URL outright…
NNS_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:6488
# …or leave it blank and set these instead. Our node listens on 6488, not the
# documented default of 8648.
NNS_RPC_HOST=
NNS_RPC_PORT=
NNS_RPC_SCHEME=http

# HTTP basic auth, from the [rpc-server] section of the node's client.toml.
# Leave both blank if the node has no credentials configured.
NNS_RPC_USER=
NNS_RPC_PASSWORD=

# ── API base URL (required by all three) ─────────────────────────────────────
# `p`: one §10.6 bound is relative — the commission may move at most
# COMMISSION_MAX_STEP from the one in effect — and GET /params answers it,
# stamped with the height it read at; no node knows it.
# `f`: the §10.2 ceiling (owed − burned) comes from GET /burn, and a burn
# without a ceiling is a burn nothing checks. Same stamp, same reason.
# `u`: whether the name is still RESERVED is chain state — GET /available/{name}
# — and a U for a name that is registered, in grace, already released or never
# on the list is mined and forfeited as NAME_NOT_RESERVED. `u` ran without this
# until 2026-08-21, and a `u nimiq` forfeited in block 59478946 to prove it.
NNS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
